  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer array numsnumsnums, find the **subarray** with the largest sum, and print its sum.\n\n**Note**: A subarray is a contiguous non-empty sequence of elements within an array.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains TTT, the number of test cases.\nThe first line in each test case contains NNN, the number of elements in an array.\nThe second line in each test case contains NNN integers, denoting the elements in the array.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum subarray sum of each array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 100",
      "1 <= N <= 100",
      "-1000000000 <= A_i <= 1000000000",
      "The answer fits in a signed 64‑bit integer"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "First line contains an integer T, the number of test cases. For each test case, the first line contains an integer N, the size of the array. The second line contains N space‑separated integers denoting the array elements.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, output a single line containing the maximum possible sum of any non‑empty contiguous subarray.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n9\n-2 1 -3 4 -1 2 1 -5 4\n1\n1\n5\n5 4 -1 7 8",
        "output": "6\n1\n23",
        "explanation": "Test case 1: maximum subarray is [4, -1, 2, 1] with sum 6.\nTest case 2: only element 1, sum 1.\nTest case 3: subarray [5, 4, -1, 7, 8] gives sum 23."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\\n5\\n-5 -2 -3 -4 -1",
        "output": "-1",
        "explanation": "All numbers are negative; the largest (least negative) single element is -1, which is the maximum subarray sum."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n1\n0",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Single element zero forms the only subarray, sum is 0."
      }
    ]
  },
