  "solution": {
    "approach": "The problem asks for the maximum sum over all contiguous subarrays. The optimal solution is Kadane's algorithm, which scans the array while maintaining the best subarray ending at the current position (cur) and the overall best seen so far (best). For each element x, the best subarray ending at x is either x alone or cur+x, i.e., cur = max(x, cur+x). The answer is the maximum cur observed. This runs in linear time and uses O(1) extra space.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(N) per test case, O(total N) over all test cases.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) auxiliary space.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.util.*;public class Main{public static void main(String[] args){Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);sc.useDelimiter(\"\\\\s+|\\\\\\\\n\");int T=sc.nextInt();StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();while(T-- >0){int N=sc.nextInt();long cur=sc.nextLong();long best=cur;for(int i=1;i<N;i++){long val=sc.nextLong();cur=Math.max(val,cur+val);if(cur>best)best=cur;}sb.append(best).append('\\n');}System.out.print(sb.toString());}}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
